    "explanation": "The fare you were charged stands, and the refund you asked for is not due. The reason is the baseline the claim uses. Trip TRP-00804 is a RYDE_POOL trip, so under POL-RD-12 the figure the route-deviation test runs against is the platform-matched pooled itinerary of 4.75 km stored on EV-TRIP-00804, not the solo-rider estimate of 3.10 km in your claim. The solo figure is carried on the record for reference only, and the clause says a claim measured against it cites the wrong field; the driver's and your own advocate's briefs both correct this. Measured the right way, EV-GPS-00804 records a trace of 4.88 km over a clean export (79 fixes, 10-second sampling, 100% coverage, no gaps), giving an excess of 0.13 km, or 2.74% of the optimal route. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to be greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms, and neither limb is met, so no route deviation is established on this trip. The distance used to collect the co-rider at Queenstown is separately excluded from excess by POL-RD-12, so the collection itself is not a deviation in law however inconvenient it was. The arithmetic confirms the point from the other direction: on EV-FARE-00804 the charged_total is SGD 11.90 and the recomputed optimal-route fare is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 4.75 + 0.28 x 14.0) x 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee = SGD 12.0825, so the refund under POL-RD-02 is charged_total less recomputed_fare, floored at zero — SGD 0.00, below the SGD 0.50 de minimis. No billing-integrity correction is available under POL-RD-09(4): the fare breakdown carries no ERP gantry lines, no tolls and no airport surcharge, and the SGD 0.80 platform fee is a standard line of the fare model, so there is no unmatched charge to refund. There is no repeat-deviation pattern under POL-RD-06 — the driver's deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 300 completed trips in the same window, well under both triggers — so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral arises. The only impaired artifact in the bundle is the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00804-01 (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0); it can carry no fact, and because nobody asserts an external traffic cause for this trip, its absence decides nothing and POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged. No driver compensation is due either: the billed distance of 4.88 km equals the trace distance, so there is no unbilled shortfall. The route-deviation claim is therefore dismissed on the evidence: under POL-GEN-03 the present state stands, the charge remains in place and nothing is refunded. Confidence is 0.95, capped by the weight-1.0 artifacts (EV-GPS-00804, EV-TRIP-00804, EV-FARE-00804) that carry the deciding measurements; the monetary effect is nil, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold. This ruling is provisional, and either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
